    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (71.99) headline our lineup as the must-start anchors. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from an excellent matchup against Valdez, with a favorable park adjustment and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery profile that elevates his stolen base potential to an elite level. **Daulton Varsho** earns his high marks through a massive 18% SP skill boost against Houser, further bolstered by his dynamic platoon advantage and high-volume SB opportunity. We are also leaning heavily into **Jonathan Aranda** (64.00) and **Gleyber Torres** (61.97); **Jonathan Aranda** is seeing a +12% bump from a favorable platoon matchup, while **Gleyber Torres** maximizes his value in the leadoff spot against a left-handed pitcher, where his efficiency spikes significantly.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Gavin Sheets** (47.64) out of the starting nine. He narrowly missed the cut due to the density of higher-projected hitters in our utility and outfield slots, specifically failing to outpace the base efficiency of **Justin Crawford** (51.91), despite the latter\u2019s disadvantageous 9-hole placement. Elsewhere, we are keeping a close eye on the risk profiles of our outfielders: while **Lawrence Butler** (55.35) remains in the lineup, his upside is severely dampened by an abysmal -19% SP skill adjustment against Rasmussen. We are accepting this volatility to prioritize his ceiling, but managers should monitor if his at-bats are shortened if the game gets out of hand early. No major weather flags are present, but the lack of official lineup confirmation for some spots means we are banking on historical tendencies for **Justin Crawford** and others in the lower third of the order.",
